VIOLATION S497: cell `anchor` changed in place
  old: §DESCRIPTION; man-pages 6.19, page dated 2026-02-08 (text copy `.ufo/waves/round-50/c1/PR_SET_PDEATHSIG.2const.txt`)
  new: §DESCRIPTION; man-pages 6.19, page dated 2026-02-08 (text copy `.ufo/waves/round-50/c1/PR_SET_PDEATHSIG.2const.txt`, sha256 `906bbe5cc7e38c02a82bb60ff3b7e0d1cfb21089a1a24f00f045fb1b86edb1e4`)
VIOLATION S497: cell `teaches` changed in place
  old: "The parent-death signal is sent upon subsequent termination of the parent thread and also upon termination of each subreaper process ... to which the caller is subsequently reparented." — so a replay and its live child can make the whole tree die when the process that started them dies
  new: "The parent-death signal is sent upon subsequent termination of the parent thread and also upon termination of each subreaper process" and "The parent-death signal setting is cleared for the child of a fork(2)." — so a replay and its live child can make the whole tree die when the process that started them dies, but only because each link sets its own signal: the kernel clears the setting across fork(2)
VIOLATION S498: cell `scope` changed in place
  old: what opens and closes a fenced code block: at least three backticks or tildes, up to three spaces of indentation, a closing fence of the same character with at least as many of them; an unclosed fence runs to the end of the containing block; the content is literal text
  new: what opens and closes a fenced code block: at least three backticks or tildes (not mixed), up to three spaces of indentation, a backtick fence whose info string holds no backtick, a closing fence of the same character with at least as many of them; an unclosed fence runs to the end of the containing block; the content is literal text
VIOLATION S498: cell `anchor` changed in place
  old: §4.5 Fenced code blocks (text copy `.ufo/waves/round-50/c2/commonmark-0.31.2-s4.5.txt`)
  new: §4.5 Fenced code blocks (text copy `.ufo/waves/round-50/c2/commonmark-0.31.2-s4.5.txt`; full page sha256 `c85f56cc2101f761cc94215c677cd2c7c1ecca9c47be016479fdfe718af60f0d`)
VIOLATION S498: cell `teaches` changed in place
  old: "A code fence is a sequence of at least three consecutive backtick characters or tildes." — so a section scanner must not treat a `## ` line inside a fence as a heading
  new: "A code fence is a sequence of at least three consecutive backtick characters (&#96;) or tildes (~)." and "The content of a code fence is treated as literal text, not parsed as inlines." — so a section scanner must not treat a `## ` line inside a fence as a heading
2 append-only violation(s)
